CiukiOS Wine 10.0: kernelbase-compile-in
Pinned base: b073859675060c9211fcbccfd90e4e87520dc2c2
Modified by CiukiOS, 2026-10-20. LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Windows 98 has no KERNELBASE; its SHLWAPI implemented the Path/Str/Url/
SHReg*US/Chr/IsChar/Hash exports itself. Compile the upstream kernelbase
path.c and string.c into SHLWAPI, plus QISearch/GetAcceptLanguages
(kernelbase/main.c) and the USKEY section of kernelbase/registry.c,
unchanged; IsChar*W over GetStringTypeW; the NT native
RtlDowncaseUnicodeChar over CharLowerW and IsDBCSLeadByteEx (not a CiukiOS
KERNEL32 export) over GetCPInfo; drop
-import for these exports; SHLWAPI imports KERNEL32 (default) and VERSION
instead of KERNELBASE. OLE32 gets PathCchFindExtension (kernelbase/path.c,
unchanged).

